---
/**
 * /design, an entry page's parts: the three boxes, the block with its prompt
 * card and Copy, and the one button. Synthetic content, shipped components.
 */
import EntryBlock from "../EntryBlock.astro";
import EntrySection from "../EntrySection.astro";
import { block } from "../../lib/reader.mjs";

const specimen = block({
  best_for: "Anyone who hands a first draft to an agent.",
  tip: "Ask for the plan before the code. Read the plan, then let it write.",
  time: { text: "10 minutes", source: "estimate" },
  needs: ["an agent", "a repo"],
  prompt: { text: "Before you write any code, write plan.md: the goal, the steps, and how you'll check each one.", ours: true },
  start_here: ["Open the repo in your agent.", "Paste the prompt.", "Read plan.md before you say go."],
});
---

<section>
  <h2 class="sheet__head mono">Entries</h2>
  <p>
    A library entry is up to three boxes, so you can see who wrote what. Written
    by AI holds what the agents drafted. In my words holds only what I typed, and
    is left out when there's nothing. The source holds the piece's own words.
  </p>

  <EntrySection level="h3" label="Written by AI" id="design-ai" icon="ai" copy>
    <dl>
      <div class="fact tldr">
        <dt>TLDR</dt>
        <dd>Plans written by the agent beat plans written for it.</dd>
      </div>
      <EntryBlock block={specimen} />
    </dl>
  </EntrySection>

  <EntrySection level="h3" label="In my words" id="design-mine" icon="pen">
    <dl>
      <div class="fact">
        <dt>Raindrop note</dt>
        <dd>Try this on the next site ticket.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </EntrySection>

  <EntrySection level="h3" label="The source" id="design-source">
    <div class="sec__body">
      <a class="ext ctl press" href="https://github.com/aayushmanchanda2/aayushmanchanda.com/blob/main/design.md" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Read design.md</a>
    </div>
  </EntrySection>

  <p>
    Copy always does something. It tries the clipboard, then a hidden field and
    the copy command inside the same click, then selects the text and says
    "Press ⌘C". Block your clipboard and press Copy above to see the last step.
  </p>
  <p>
    There's one button, <span class="code">.ctl</span>: 32px, a hairline box, 14px
    secondary ink, 40px of target (44 under a finger). Copy and "Read the full
    article" both use it. Controls in a bar or a caption stay text.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .tldr dd {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
</style>
